Well, that that would explain it.
嗯，那倒是能解释得通。

1090
00:46:16.430 --> 00:46:17.530
Yes, that would explain it.
没错，那样就能解释通了。

1091
00:46:17.710 --> 00:46:20.630
We had a fan question from Alexa Porter.
我们收到一个粉丝亚历克莎·波特的提问。

1092
00:46:21.010 --> 00:46:24.050
Was there ever talk of putting Pam and Roy back together?
有没有讨论过让帕姆和罗伊复合？

1093
00:46:24.050 --> 00:46:27.010
Or was it all just a setup to mess with our feelings?
还是说这一切只是为了戏弄我们的感情？

1094
00:46:27.910 --> 00:46:33.530
Well, there was talk in the writer's room that maybe Roy could win Pam back.
编剧室里确实讨论过罗伊或许能追回帕姆。

1095
00:46:33.530 --> 00:46:37.690
Remember, David Denman was made a series regular for season three.
别忘了，大卫·丹曼在第三季成了常驻演员。

1096
00:46:38.110 --> 00:46:38.250
Yeah.
没错。

1097
00:46:38.990 --> 00:46:42.390
So he's going to be making a lot of appearances this season.
所以这一季他会频繁出现。

1098
00:46:42.390 --> 00:46:48.870
And I can tell you guys, nothing was decided at this point about what would happen with Jim
我可以告诉大家，当时关于吉姆和帕姆会怎样，帕姆和罗伊会怎样，

1099
00:46:48.870 --> 00:46:50.850
and Pam, what would happen with Pam and Roy.
还没有任何定论。

1100
00:46:51.090 --> 00:46:53.130
They were feeling it out week to week.
他们当时也是走一步看一步。

1101
00:46:53.410 --> 00:46:55.070
I totally remember that.
我完全记得那件事。

1102
00:46:55.070 --> 00:47:01.330
But I also remember it was constantly said that maybe, maybe in the series of The Office,
但我还记得当时一直有人说，或许，或许在《办公室》这部剧里，

1103
00:47:01.610 --> 00:47:07.510
Jim and Pam would not end up together in the end, but would instead lead one another to
吉姆和帕姆最后并不会在一起，而是会各自走向

1104
00:47:07.510 --> 00:47:08.910
their actual true loves.
他们真正的挚爱。

1105
00:47:09.330 --> 00:47:14.310
There was, it had not been decided right now that Jim and Pam were one another's true loves.
当时还没定下来吉姆和帕姆就是彼此的挚爱。

1106
00:47:14.310 --> 00:47:16.650
When you just said that, I got angry.
你刚才那么一说，我都有点生气了。

1107
00:47:16.990 --> 00:47:17.670
Oh, no.
噢，别这样。

1108
00:47:17.950 --> 00:47:20.150
I was like, no, Jim and Pam.
我当时心想，不，吉姆和帕姆必须在一起。

1109
00:47:23.140 --> 00:47:28.400
Well, I think maybe that's why the writing of their characters felt so authentic,
嗯，我想这也许就是为什么他们角色的塑造感觉如此真实，

1110
00:47:28.400 --> 00:47:33.720
because the writers were figuring out their relationship at the same time that Jim and Pam were.
因为编剧们在构思他们关系的同时，吉姆和帕姆也在经历着同样的过程。

1111
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:34.580
Yeah.
没错。

1112
00:47:34.720 --> 00:47:38.220
So we're, as an audience, we feel that like, what will happen?
所以作为观众，我们也会感到好奇，接下来会发生什么？

1113
00:47:38.400 --> 00:47:39.020
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1114
00:47:39.180 --> 00:47:41.980
These are two people on journeys trying to find themselves.
他们是两个正在寻找自我的旅人。

1115
00:47:42.120 --> 00:47:44.380
And hopefully that leads them back to each other.
希望这最终能让他们回到彼此身边。

1116
00:47:44.380 --> 00:47:45.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1117
00:47:45.660 --> 00:47:46.100
Exactly.
确实如此。

1118
00:47:46.500 --> 00:47:46.860
All right.
好吧。

1119
00:47:47.100 --> 00:47:53.240
So while Pam and Roy are out in the parking lot, I'm sure Pam was really hoping that she's
所以当帕姆和罗伊在停车场时，我敢肯定帕姆真的很希望

1120
00:47:53.240 --> 00:47:57.320
going to come back to the conference room and the grief counseling's almost over.
她回到会议室时，悲伤辅导已经快结束了。

1121
00:47:57.420 --> 00:48:00.280
But no, they waited for her because they're a family.
但并没有，他们一直在等她，因为他们是一家人。

1122
00:48:00.860 --> 00:48:02.320
They waited for her.
他们一直在等她。

1123
00:48:02.420 --> 00:48:02.740
Yes.
是的。

1124
00:48:02.980 --> 00:48:05.020
There's a great scene on the DVD.
DVD里有一个很棒的片段。

1125
00:48:05.760 --> 00:48:07.000
It's a deleted scene.
那是一个删减片段。

1126
00:48:07.120 --> 00:48:10.900
And Michael is trying to get everyone to loosen up, right, for the grief counseling.
迈克尔当时正试图让大家放松下来，为了悲伤辅导，对吧。

1127
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:13.980
He's like, hey, guys, take your jackets off, loosen your ties,
他说，嘿，伙计们，脱掉外套，松开领带，

1128
00:48:13.980 --> 00:48:15.000
guys, take off your shoes.
伙计们，把鞋脱了。

1129
00:48:15.140 --> 00:48:16.580
Ladies, let your hair down.
女士们，把头发散下来。

1130
00:48:17.260 --> 00:48:20.880
And Angela goes, I don't think Kevin should take off his shoes.
然后安吉拉说，我觉得凯文不该脱鞋。

1131
00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:23.020
Oh!
噢！

1132
00:48:23.320 --> 00:48:25.380
And Kevin gets really annoyed.
凯文变得非常恼火。

1133
00:48:25.440 --> 00:48:33.020
And then he has a talking head that he says, all right, listen, I have hyperhidrosis, okay?
然后他有一个采访镜头，他说，好吧，听着，我有手足多汗症，好吗？

1134
00:48:34.900 --> 00:48:41.320
So we find out that he has this disease that makes your feet sweat really, really badly.
所以我们发现他患有这种会让脚出汗非常非常严重的疾病。

1135
00:48:41.580 --> 00:48:45.160
So I guess he's been taking his shoes off over in accounting.
所以我猜他在会计部那边一直都有脱鞋的习惯。

1136
00:48:45.160 --> 00:48:46.980
I love this little tidbit.
我喜欢这个小花絮。

1137
00:48:47.160 --> 00:48:48.740
And I'm sad it didn't make it in.
很遗憾它没能出现在正片里。

1138
00:48:48.880 --> 00:48:55.280
Well, this explains why when Pam walks into the room, Kevin's feet are up on her chair and
嗯，这就解释了为什么当帕姆走进房间时，凯文的脚放在她的椅子上，

1139
00:48:55.280 --> 00:48:56.280
his shoes are off.
而且鞋子是脱掉的。

1140
00:48:56.280 --> 00:48:58.540
Yes, people wrote in and asked about that.
是的，有人写信问过这件事。

1141
00:48:58.540 --> 00:49:02.560
It's because in the deleted scene, Michael is getting everyone to loosen up.
那是因为在删减片段里，迈克尔让大家放松下来。

1142
00:49:02.700 --> 00:49:05.660
And we find out that Kevin has, how do you say it?
然后我们发现凯文有，那个词怎么说来着？

1143
00:49:06.520 --> 00:49:07.000
Hyperhidrosis.
多汗症。

1144
00:49:07.200 --> 00:49:08.360
Angela, I love that.
安吉拉，我喜欢这个。

1145
00:49:08.480 --> 00:49:09.860
That's a good catch.
观察得很仔细。

1146
00:49:10.040 --> 00:49:10.940
That's a good catch.
观察得很仔细。

1147
00:49:11.060 --> 00:49:11.520
Good tip.
好建议。

1148
00:49:11.720 --> 00:49:12.120
Tidbit.
小花絮。

1149
00:49:12.280 --> 00:49:12.680
Tidbit.
小花絮。

1150
00:49:12.780 --> 00:49:13.640
It's a Kinsey tidbit.
这是一个金赛小花絮。

1151
00:49:13.880 --> 00:49:14.220
All right.
好的。

1152
00:49:14.360 --> 00:49:18.800
So when Pam does finally get back, they begin again.
所以当帕姆终于回来时，他们又开始了。

1153
00:49:18.980 --> 00:49:21.080
And Dwight is the first one to share.
德怀特是第一个分享的人。

1154
00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:24.120
Oh, this is one of my favorite things.
噢，这是我最喜欢的事情之一。

1155
00:49:24.360 --> 00:49:31.440
And Dwight shares that he was supposed to have a twin, but he absorbed the twin in utero.
德怀特分享说他本该有个双胞胎兄弟，但他还在子宫里时就把对方吸收了。

1156
00:49:32.340 --> 00:49:32.680
All right.
好的。

1157
00:49:32.720 --> 00:49:34.840
We had a fan question from Aira Tajali.
我们收到了一个来自艾拉·塔贾利的粉丝提问。

1158
00:49:35.080 --> 00:49:40.760
Did Rainn Wilson make the whole absorbing twin thing up or was it scripted?
雷恩·威尔森关于吸收双胞胎的事是即兴发挥的，还是剧本里写的？

1159
00:49:41.560 --> 00:49:45.620
Well, first of all, I will tell you, it is not in the script.
嗯，首先，我可以告诉你，剧本里没有这一段。

1160
00:49:46.360 --> 00:49:51.360
I don't know if Rainn made it up, but in the script, Dwight was supposed to say this.
我不知道是不是雷恩编的，但在剧本里，德怀特原本应该说的是这个。

1161
00:49:51.560 --> 00:49:58.220
He was supposed to say, in the blizzard of 97, 12 shroots died in the basement of our house.
他原本应该说，在97年的那场暴风雪中，有12个施鲁特家的人死在了我们家的地下室里。

1162
00:49:58.520 --> 00:50:01.380
They drank beer cider that had already turned.
他们喝了已经变质的苹果酒。

1163
00:50:02.080 --> 00:50:04.900
President McKinley declared it a national emergency.
麦金莱总统宣布那是一场国家紧急状态。

1164
00:50:06.120 --> 00:50:09.660
Now, my favorite thing about that is that clearly it's not 1997.
现在，关于那段话我最喜欢的一点是，显然那不是1997年。

1165
00:50:11.680 --> 00:50:13.300
It's like 1897.
那听起来像是1897年。

1166
00:50:13.560 --> 00:50:13.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1167
00:50:13.980 --> 00:50:14.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1168
00:50:14.580 --> 00:50:15.360
I guess.
我想是吧。

1169
00:50:16.180 --> 00:50:19.920
But that was originally Dwight's grief share.
但那原本是德怀特的悲伤分享内容。

1170
00:50:20.240 --> 00:50:21.600
So here's the thing.
所以重点来了。

1171
00:50:21.820 --> 00:50:27.120
I reached out to Jen Salata about this, and this is maybe one of my favorite text threads of all time.
我为此联系了简·萨拉塔，这可能是我有史以来最喜欢的短信对话之一。

1172
00:50:27.320 --> 00:50:32.240
This is what tickled me so much is that Jen Salata, Jenna, she's one of our people.
最让我觉得有趣的是，简·萨拉塔，珍娜，她是我们的自己人。

1173
00:50:32.480 --> 00:50:33.460
She's a deep diver.
她是个深挖细节的人。

1174
00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:39.400
She is a deep, the minute I asked her, she went on a deep dive for the whole afternoon.
她真的很深入，我一问她，她就花了一整个下午去深挖这件事。

1175
00:50:39.580 --> 00:50:39.720
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1176
00:50:40.180 --> 00:50:45.260
So I say, okay, Jen, Dwight's speech about absorbing his twin is not in the script.
所以我说，好吧，简，德怀特关于吸收双胞胎的演讲不在剧本里。

1177
00:50:45.440 --> 00:50:46.380
Was that an improv?
那是即兴表演吗？

1178
00:50:46.560 --> 00:50:47.520
Did you tell him on the day?
是你当天告诉他的吗？

1179
00:50:47.700 --> 00:50:50.700
She goes, oh my God, I don't remember.
她说，天哪，我不记得了。

1180
00:50:50.900 --> 00:50:52.200
Oh my God, I love that speech.
天哪，我太喜欢那段演讲了。

1181
00:50:52.360 --> 00:50:53.760
And sadly, it wasn't mine.
遗憾的是，那不是我想出来的。

1182
00:50:54.160 --> 00:50:55.800
I'm going to start texting people.
我要开始给别人发短信了。

1183
00:50:56.020 --> 00:50:56.640
Please hold.
请稍等。

1184
00:50:57.660 --> 00:50:59.120
Oh, I love this so much.
噢，我太喜欢这个过程了。

1185
00:50:59.120 --> 00:51:00.260
This happened throughout the day.
这事儿发生在一整天里。

1186
00:51:00.400 --> 00:51:01.620
She said, I texted Rain.
她说，我发短信问了雷恩。

1187
00:51:01.620 --> 00:51:05.220
Rain actually thinks it was an alt pitched from Paul.
雷恩其实觉得那是保罗提议的备选方案。

1188
00:51:06.340 --> 00:51:07.920
Jen said, here's a side note.
简说，顺便提一下。

1189
00:51:08.100 --> 00:51:13.660
I had a friend that reabsorbed his twin, but I definitely didn't come up with the strength of a baby.
我有个朋友确实重新吸收了他的双胞胎，但我绝对没想出“婴儿的力量”这种说法。

1190
00:51:15.200 --> 00:51:17.900
She said, I'm going to check with Paul where that part came from.
她说，我要去问问保罗那部分是从哪来的。

1191
00:51:18.080 --> 00:51:18.820
Please hold.
请稍等。

1192
00:51:19.020 --> 00:51:19.840
She texts Paul.
她给保罗发了短信。

1193
00:51:20.340 --> 00:51:22.760
Paul says he thinks it was Justin Spitzer.
保罗说他觉得是贾斯汀·斯皮策想出来的。

1194
00:51:23.040 --> 00:51:23.920
Hold one second.
等一下。

1195
00:51:24.220 --> 00:51:25.360
Now texting Justin.
现在在给贾斯汀发短信。

1196
00:51:25.620 --> 00:51:27.120
Justin was another one of our writers.
贾斯汀是我们另一位编剧。

1197
00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:29.840
This is what Justin texted Jen back.
这是贾斯汀回复简的短信内容。

1198
00:51:30.080 --> 00:51:35.500
I still remember that because it was early season three and I was so nervous about proving myself.
我还记得那件事，因为那是第三季早期，我当时非常紧张，急于证明自己。

1199
00:51:35.800 --> 00:51:38.040
I guess, yes, I came up with it.
我想，是的，是我编出来的。

1200
00:51:38.160 --> 00:51:45.360
But the thing that really sold it to me was the last line about him having the strength of a grown man plus a baby.
但真正打动我的是最后那句关于他拥有成年人外加一个婴儿的力量。

1201
00:51:45.360 --> 00:51:49.020
And that was something that Paul Lieberstein added after.
那是保罗·利伯斯坦后来加进去的。

1202
00:51:49.260 --> 00:51:52.320
So I think he deserves a fair amount of credit as well.
所以我认为他也理应获得相当多的赞誉。

1203
00:51:55.610 --> 00:51:57.590
So I'm giving that a slow clap.
所以我决定为他献上慢速鼓掌。

1204
00:51:57.890 --> 00:51:57.990
A slow clap.
慢速鼓掌。

1205
00:51:58.210 --> 00:51:59.970
Into a big clap.
然后变成热烈鼓掌。

1206
00:52:00.330 --> 00:52:00.750
Yes.
没错。

1207
00:52:01.670 --> 00:52:02.190
Wow.
哇。

1208
00:52:02.450 --> 00:52:04.950
It was a two-hander that Paul and Justin pitched.
那是保罗和贾斯汀共同提出的双人戏份。

1209
00:52:05.230 --> 00:52:11.210
I love that we got to the bottom of that mystery because it is one of my all-time favorite Dwight-isMs.
我很高兴我们查清了那个谜团，因为那是我最喜欢的德怀特语录之一。

1210
00:52:12.050 --> 00:52:16.590
Also, guys, Justin Spitzer is the creator of the show Superstore.
另外，伙计们，贾斯汀·斯皮策是《爆笑超市》这部剧的创作者。

1211
00:52:16.590 --> 00:52:19.010
Justin is so talented.
贾斯汀非常有才华。

1212
00:52:19.290 --> 00:52:20.210
He's so talented.
他太有才了。

1213
00:52:20.390 --> 00:52:20.750
I love him.
我爱死他了。

1214
00:52:20.870 --> 00:52:21.290
Love him.
爱他。

1215
00:52:21.830 --> 00:52:22.330
Anyway.
总之。

1216
00:52:22.690 --> 00:52:27.290
I think the only place to go from here is back to our grief circle.
我觉得接下来我们只能回到悲伤辅导圈了。

1217
00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:29.890
And we need to hear from some others.
我们需要听听其他人的想法。

1218
00:52:30.350 --> 00:52:30.590
Okay.
好的。

1219
00:52:30.670 --> 00:52:34.570
So we're back into the grief counseling scene and Stanley has just refused.
我们回到了悲伤辅导的场景，斯坦利刚刚拒绝了。

1220
00:52:34.570 --> 00:52:36.210
He is not going to participate.
他不打算参与。

1221
00:52:36.470 --> 00:52:36.610
No.
不。

1222
00:52:37.070 --> 00:52:38.810
He chunks that ball back at Michael.
他把球扔回给了迈克尔。

1223
00:52:39.270 --> 00:52:39.710
Hey.
嘿。

1224
00:52:39.810 --> 00:52:40.410
I heard that.
我听到了。

1225
00:52:40.570 --> 00:52:41.330
Yeah, you heard that.
没错，你听到了。

1226
00:52:41.350 --> 00:52:41.690
I heard that.
我听到了。

1227
00:52:41.950 --> 00:52:43.750
But Pam agrees to participate.
但帕姆同意参与。

1228
00:52:43.750 --> 00:52:46.770
And she's going to share a story about her family.
她打算分享一个关于她家庭的故事。

1229
00:52:46.970 --> 00:52:51.290
But it's clearly just the synopsis for the movie Million Dollar Baby.
但那显然只是电影《百万美元宝贝》的剧情梗概。

1230
00:52:52.130 --> 00:52:54.330
I mean, again, Pam is now the gem.
我是说，帕姆现在真是个宝藏。

1231
00:52:54.570 --> 00:52:55.390
She's the jokester.
她是那个爱开玩笑的人。

1232
00:52:56.090 --> 00:52:56.610
Yes.
没错。

1233
00:52:56.850 --> 00:53:02.610
And then Ryan joins in and he shares a story that is very clearly the Lion King.
然后瑞安也加入了，他分享的故事显然是《狮子王》。

1234
00:53:02.910 --> 00:53:04.710
I mean, he says the word Mufasa.
我是说，他甚至说出了“木法沙”这个词。

1235
00:53:05.110 --> 00:53:06.490
I mean, come on.
拜托，别闹了。

1236
00:53:06.490 --> 00:53:10.270
But then Kevin catches on and he's tickled.
但凯文领会到了，他觉得很有趣。

1237
00:53:10.470 --> 00:53:11.450
He wants to participate.
他想参与进来。

1238
00:53:11.450 --> 00:53:12.750
He wants to play the game.
他想玩这个游戏。

1239
00:53:12.890 --> 00:53:15.310
But he goes too broad, too on the nose.
但他讲得太宽泛，太直白了。

1240
00:53:15.470 --> 00:53:17.890
And he basically breaks down Weekend at Bernie's.
