我想那是因为我们在户外。

1768
01:15:47.030 --> 01:15:49.090
It was because we had a bird funeral.
那是因为我们举行了一场鸟儿葬礼。

1769
01:15:50.010 --> 01:15:58.910
It was so exciting for the amazing sound people, who do a fantastic job, to put a lot of bird noises in.
对于那些出色的音效师来说，能加入大量的鸟叫声一定非常令人兴奋，他们做得太棒了。

1770
01:15:58.910 --> 01:16:09.950
And because for the longest time, when we're inside the office, they're just putting dot matrix printer sounds and just faxes and old-fashioned office noises.
因为在很长一段时间里，当我们待在办公室里时，他们只能加入针式打印机的声音、传真声和老式的办公室噪音。

1771
01:16:09.950 --> 01:16:18.510
So, it must have been such a treat and a field day to be able to go outside and hear birds, and especially on theme with the funeral.
所以，能够去户外听到鸟叫声，尤其是与葬礼主题相符，对他们来说一定是一种享受和狂欢。

1772
01:16:18.850 --> 01:16:29.290
So, I remember, it was a slight exaggeration, but it sounded a little bit like Alfred Hitchcock, the birds, when I first heard the playback for the bird funeral.
我记得，虽然有点夸张，但当我第一次听到鸟儿葬礼的录音时，听起来有点像阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的《群鸟》。

1773
01:16:29.290 --> 01:16:35.290
But they quickly made a wonderful adjustment, and it was the right amount of outside birds.
但他们很快做出了极好的调整，那才是户外鸟叫声的正确音量。

1774
01:16:36.590 --> 01:16:37.570
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

1775
01:16:37.710 --> 01:16:39.930
I love that our sound mixers got so excited.
我喜欢我们的混音师们如此兴奋。

1776
